       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, which is about 3.75 times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. At that dose it risks serious liver injury and liver failure. It's also well above a normal single dose of 500\u20131000 mg.\n\nI suspect a typo or a unit mix-up. Two common options for a 70 kg adult with normal liver function are:\n\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, which is 2.6 g/day\n- **1000 mg PO three times daily**, which is 3 g/day\n- The maximum is 1000 mg PO four times daily, which is 4 g/day\n\nTell me which dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it. If you really do intend 5000 mg TID, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending and with pharmacy first. I'd also want to know the clinical reason, such as whether this is a formulation or unit error."
      }
