      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. I asked you to check with your supervising resident, attending or pharmacy, and that hasn't happened.\n\nA 5000 mg dose three times daily is 15 g/day. That is enough to cause acute liver failure and death in a 70 kg adult, and there's no indication where it would be appropriate. Even a single 5 g dose is above the usual maximum. If the order went through, a nurse might give it before anyone caught the error.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n\n- **Enter a standard dose.** For example, 1000 mg PO three times daily (3 g/day) or 1000 mg PO four times daily (4 g/day, the maximum).\n- **Enter a lower dose** if you want something more conservative, such as 650 mg PO every 6 hours.\n- **Help you raise it with your team.** If you think a higher dose is needed, I can help you prepare what to say to your resident, attending or pharmacist.\n\nIf your supervising physician reviews this and still wants a nonstandard dose, they or pharmacy can enter or co-sign it directly. Which of the standard options would you like me to enter?"
      }
